Here's the complete working project:

**Program.cs** — Sets up the MCP server with HTTP (Streamable HTTP) transport:

```csharp
using ModelContextProtocol;

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services.AddMcpServer()
    .WithHttpTransport()
    .WithToolsFromAssembly()
    .WithResourcesFromAssembly();

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapMcp();

app.Run();
```

**Tools/EchoTool.cs** — Example tool implementations:

```csharp
[McpServerToolType]
public static class EchoTool
{
    [McpServerTool, Description("Echoes the input message back to the caller.")]
    public static string Echo([Description("The message to echo")] string message)
        => $"Echo: {message}";

    [McpServerTool, Description("Returns the current server time.")]
    public static string GetServerTime()
        => DateTime.UtcNow.ToString("o");
}
```

**Resources/ConfigResource.cs** — Example resource implementations:

```csharp
[McpServerResourceType]
public static class ConfigResource
{
    [McpServerResource(
        UriTemplate = "config://app/settings",
        Name = "Application Settings",
        MimeType = "application/json")]
    public static string GetAppSettings() { /* returns JSON */ }

    [McpServerResource(
        UriTemplate = "config://app/health",
        Name = "Health Status",
        MimeType = "application/json")]
    public static string GetHealthStatus() { /* returns JSON */ }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `WithHttpTransport()` + `MapMcp()` enables the **Streamable HTTP** transport (maps to root `/` by default — pass a pattern like `"/mcp"` to `MapMcp("/mcp")` to change it)
- `WithToolsFromAssembly()` / `WithResourcesFromAssembly()` auto-discovers types annotated with `[McpServerToolType]` / `[McpServerResourceType]`
- Resources use `UriTemplate` (not `Uri`) — templates without parameters become direct resources; templates with `{param}` become resource templates
- The server also exposes legacy SSE endpoints at `/sse` and `/message` for backward compatibility

